! DBG89F.DBG - SET SCOPE on the compiler's MACRO for a recursive function
! (README.md). FACT's N is through 4(AP), K at FACT.K(FP), so each activation's
! are reached through that scope's AP and FP. VMS's log leaves out a command
! that fails, so a comment names each case first.
SET BREAK FACT.L10
GO
SHOW CALLS
SHOW SCOPE
!> Scope 0, FACT(1)
EXAMINE AP
EXAMINE FP
!> EXAMINE .(.AP+FACT.N), N
EXAMINE .(.AP+FACT.N)
!> EXAMINE .FP+FACT.K, K
EXAMINE .FP+FACT.K
!> SET SCOPE 1, FACT(2)
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE AP
EXAMINE FP
EXAMINE .(.AP+FACT.N)
EXAMINE .FP+FACT.K
!> EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC
EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC
!> SET SCOPE 3, FACT(4)
SET SCOPE 3
EXAMINE .(.AP+FACT.N)
EXAMINE .FP+FACT.K
!> SET SCOPE 4, the main program
SET SCOPE 4
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R
EXAMINE DBG89F.R
!> Without SET SCOPE: EXAMINE 2\%FP
CANCEL SCOPE
EXAMINE 2\%FP
!> EXAMINE FACT 2\%AP
EXAMINE FACT 2\%AP
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 2, then EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 2
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC
CANCEL SCOPE
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
!> GO to the end
GO
